Lemma 25: f(W, f(f(W, f(Y, f(Z, W))), W)) = f(X, f(f(X, f(Y, f(Z, X))), X)).
Proof:
  f(W, f(f(W, f(Y, f(Z, W))), W))
= { by lemma 16 R->L }
  f(W, f(f(W, f(Y, f(f(f(f(Z, V), f(V, f(f(V, Z), f(Z, V)))), f(Z, V)), W))), W))
= { by lemma 18 }
  f(X, f(f(X, f(Y, f(f(f(f(Z, V), f(V, f(f(V, Z), f(Z, V)))), f(Z, V)), X))), X))
= { by lemma 16 }
